    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald Feeney West are delighted to present this distinctive detached bungalow to the market, ideally located in the highly sought-after residential area of Bohernasup, Ballina. Extending to approximately 1,819 sq. ft. (169 sq. m.), this spacious property offers excellent potential and, while requiring renovation, provides an outstanding opportunity to create a superb family home.\n\nBohernasup is widely regarded as one of Ballina's most desirable residential locations. Situated just 500 yards from the town centre, the property enjoys exceptional convenience, with a wide range of amenities within easy walking distance, including shops, restaurants, cafés, bars, churches, schools, the library, and excellent public transport links via bus and rail.\n\nThe accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall, a bright sitting room with an open fireplace, a kitchen, and a dining room. French doors from the living area open onto a deck overlooking the generous south-west-facing rear garden, creating an ideal space for outdoor entertaining. There are four spacious double bedrooms, a family bathroom, and a second bathroom. Additional storage is available on the first floor.\n\nExternally, the property benefits from a large, private south-west-facing rear garden laid out in lawn, offering excellent outdoor space and plenty of scope for landscaping or extension (subject to planning permission). Off-street parking is available to the front of the property.\n\nThe property is connected to all mains services and is heated by oil-fired central heating.\n\nIdeally positioned, the property is approximately 14 km from the seaside village of Enniscrone, 39 km from Ireland West Airport Knock, and 60 km from Sligo Town.\n\nWith its generous accommodation, prime location, and enormous potential, this property represents an excellent opportunity for those seeking to create a spacious family home in one of Ballina's most established residential areas.\n\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
